### POS Ledger API — a walk through the whole thing.
### Run `docker compose up` first. In VS Code use the REST Client extension; in Rider and
### Visual Studio this file runs natively. The Swagger UI at http://localhost:8080 does the same.

@host = http://localhost:8080

### 1. Liveness — must answer without a database.
GET {{host}}/health

### 2. Readiness — this one does need the database.
GET {{host}}/ready

### 3. Sign in as the admin. Copy accessToken into @adminToken below.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/token
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "admin", "password": "admin-demo-2026" }

### 4. And as the cashier, who may sell but not touch the catalogue.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/token
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "cashier", "password": "cashier-demo-2026" }

@adminToken = paste-the-admin-token-here
@cashierToken = paste-the-cashier-token-here

### 5. The catalogue is readable without a token.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/products?limit=3

### 6. Page through it with the cursor from the previous response.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/products?limit=3&after=FLT-100

### 7. Search matches name and sku, case-insensitively.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/products?q=coffee

### 8. Creating a product needs the admin role. Without a token this is 401.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/products
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sku": "SCARCE-1", "name": "Last few units", "unitPrice": 5000.00, "initialStock": 3 }

### 9. With the cashier's token it is 403 — authenticated, but not allowed.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/products
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{cashierToken}}

{ "sku": "NOPE-1", "name": "Should not appear", "unitPrice": 100.00, "initialStock": 1 }

### 10. With the admin's token it is created, and the initial stock lands in the ledger.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/products
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{ "sku": "SCARCE-1", "name": "Last few units", "unitPrice": 5000.00, "initialStock": 3 }

### 11. The same SKU again is a 409 — the unique constraint decides, not a prior SELECT.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/products
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{ "sku": "SCARCE-1", "name": "Duplicate", "unitPrice": 5000.00, "initialStock": 1 }

### 12. Sell two of them. Replace productId with the id from step 10.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/sales
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{cashierToken}}
Idempotency-Key: 7f1c4a4e-0000-4000-8000-000000000001

{ "lines": [ { "productId": "REPLACE-WITH-PRODUCT-ID", "quantity": 2 } ] }

### 13. Send step 12 again, unchanged. Same sale, same number, stock unchanged —
### and an Idempotent-Replay: true header on the response.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/sales
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{cashierToken}}
Idempotency-Key: 7f1c4a4e-0000-4000-8000-000000000001

{ "lines": [ { "productId": "REPLACE-WITH-PRODUCT-ID", "quantity": 2 } ] }

### 14. Same key, different basket: 422. That is a client bug and hiding it helps nobody.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/sales
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{cashierToken}}
Idempotency-Key: 7f1c4a4e-0000-4000-8000-000000000001

{ "lines": [ { "productId": "REPLACE-WITH-PRODUCT-ID", "quantity": 9 } ] }

### 15. Ask for more than there is: 409, and the response names the shortfall.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/sales
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{cashierToken}}
Idempotency-Key: 7f1c4a4e-0000-4000-8000-000000000002

{ "lines": [ { "productId": "REPLACE-WITH-PRODUCT-ID", "quantity": 999 } ] }

### 16. Import a stock file. Two rows are fine, three are not, and the report says why.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/imports
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----boundary

------boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="stock.csv"
Content-Type: text/csv

sku,quantity,reason,note
CAF-500,25,Import,march restock
MUG-STD,-2,Adjustment,breakage
GHOST-1,5,Import,no such product
CAF-500,3,Import,duplicate row
MUG-STD,abc,Import,not a number
------boundary--

### 17. Reconcile: every product that moved, and any whose stock disagrees with its ledger.
### Drift must be 0 everywhere. If it is not, something wrote stock without a movement.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/reconciliation
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 18. Recent sales.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/sales?limit=10
Authorization: Bearer {{cashierToken}}
